00:03:01.039 --> 00:03:02.110
Morning!

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:03.680
I'm going to leave

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.510
with the framework of why I believe that

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.802
audio should be the biggest conversation

00:03:07.802 --> 00:03:09.823
in this conference.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:13.030
I believe that way too many people

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:15.720
make the mistake of trying to catch

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:17.570
the next technology wave

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:21.930
long before it's the
actual technology wave.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.820
There's been remarkable money lost

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:26.070
in the last three or four years

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.559
around VR and AR.

00:03:28.559 --> 00:03:31.280
Not because it's not coming,

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.930
but because the number one mistake

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:35.570
in this collective room is

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:38.691
not paying attention
to the actual consumer.

00:03:38.691 --> 00:03:41.700
We have ideologies around our technology.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.473
We are technologists and get excited

00:03:44.473 --> 00:03:46.650
about future technologies.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:49.020
But very often, over the last 20 years,

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:53.370
I have watched this ecosystem
get way too ahead of itself

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.083
without realizing that the
consumer was not ready.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.550
Nobody is home right now

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:01.790
sitting in a VR contraption

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.693
spending 10 hours a day VRing.

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:06.410
What we need to do is

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.890
be best at what is current.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:11.420
How many people here listen to a podcast?

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:12.400
Raise your hand.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.520
Raise it high.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:14.730
Look around.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.980
Now, put your hands down.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.130
How many of those people

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:19.210
that just raised their hands

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:21.100
were not listening to a podcast

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.023
just five years ago, raise your hands.

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:27.440
That is what I spend my time on.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:29.850
Where are we now?

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.651
Not four years from now.

00:04:31.651 --> 00:04:34.110
Not four years ago.

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.080
Right this second.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.230
And right this second,

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:41.800
we sit in an incredible place with audio.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:46.800
We value time and
convenience over everything.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.590
As much as the world wants us to

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:50.700
continue to value privacy,

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:55.220
every day, humans around
the world give up privacy

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:57.880
for time, speed and convenience.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.976
It's just the way we are as animals.

00:04:59.976 --> 00:05:02.750
In that insight,

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:04.765
you must understand how important

00:05:04.765 --> 00:05:08.290
your audio strategy is going forward.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:10.970
How many people here
consume YouTube videos?

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:11.803
Raise your hand.

00:05:11.803 --> 00:05:12.810
Raise it high if you do.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:13.760
Just raise it high.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.840
How many of you now, when
you watch YouTube videos

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:19.298
are starting to not even

00:05:19.298 --> 00:05:21.930
watch the video, you're just listening.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:22.980
Raise your hands.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:23.813
Look around.

00:05:23.813 --> 00:05:25.022
Keep 'em up.

00:05:25.022 --> 00:05:25.855
Look around.

00:05:25.855 --> 00:05:27.260
This, my friends,

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.000
between podcast growth,

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.190
between the fact that the
number one video platform

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:33.405
in the world is now being consumed

00:05:33.405 --> 00:05:36.470
for a shocking percentage in audio,

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:39.100
not video, is very important.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:42.060
You can imagine when I see that many hands

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:44.300
why it gets hard for
me to get excited about

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.200
video production value,

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.558
when I know the actual consumption

00:05:47.558 --> 00:05:50.690
is actually being done in audio.

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:52.830
Doesn't mean that video is declining.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.430
Video is growing!

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:56.530
Consumption is growing.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:58.720
Because we have devices
with us at all times.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.756
We don't have to go home
and watch television

00:06:00.756 --> 00:06:02.343
or the radio.

00:06:02.343 --> 00:06:04.930
I believe the number one opportunity

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.680
for the majority of this room

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:09.240
is a very strong strategy around

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:11.800
podcasting and audio content.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.980
Especially because what has emerged

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:16.005
the last 24 months,

00:06:16.005 --> 00:06:17.718
and will continue to grow

00:06:17.718 --> 00:06:21.330
is AI-driven voice devices in our homes.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:23.378
I believe that this is the

00:06:23.378 --> 00:06:28.378
end of an era where visual
and written creative

00:06:28.805 --> 00:06:31.280
can establish so much brand,

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:36.060
that it preps you for an
audio-centric brand warfare.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:40.504
I couldn't be more passionate
and push everybody here

00:06:40.504 --> 00:06:43.730
to dramatically rev up the content

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:45.425
they put out in the world.

00:06:45.425 --> 00:06:48.342
(reflective music)

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:53.980
- What's your lesson for
a modern communicator

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.341
in this era in audio?

00:06:55.341 --> 00:06:59.220
- To produce, volume has
to be put on a pedestal.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:00.053
Everybody thinks that

00:07:00.053 --> 00:07:01.070
if you make a lot of quantity,

00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:02.280
you can't make quality.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:03.560
I think it's the reverse.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.820
I think quantity leads to quality

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:06.980
because as you're putting it out,

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:09.230
you can listen to what
people are responding to,

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:10.866
and you can make better
and better content.

00:07:10.866 --> 00:07:11.893
- To made up content

00:07:11.893 --> 00:07:13.075
- [Man] Excuse me,
- Volume, yes.

00:07:13.075 --> 00:07:14.433
Yes, move, yes.

00:07:15.309 --> 00:07:17.470
- [Woman] Armenian
podcasters and YouTubers.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.083
We just started.

00:07:19.083 --> 00:07:20.014
- Make.

00:07:20.014 --> 00:07:23.510
I think the number one
mistake people are making

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:25.070
when they are a podcaster or YouTube

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:27.380
is they're overthinking
their content production,

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.730
and they're not spending
enough time on stories.

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:31.380
It's the stories that people want.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.136
Like production matters, but

00:07:33.136 --> 00:07:35.990
it's the story at the
end of the day and so,

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:38.200
more making, less thinking.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:40.040
- And what if they have already started

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:41.310
but they have no results?

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:42.230
For example, I don't know,

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:44.850
they have been doing
videos for a year or two

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:46.320
but they have no results.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.310
- The first three years I did

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:49.368
Wine Library TV, nobody was watching.

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:52.285
(reflective music)

