00:08:19.741 --> 00:08:22.320
So I think when Rogan inevitably does

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.293
Howard Stern 2.0,

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:26.340
I think you'll start
seeing people realize,

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:27.460
oh, there is something here

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:29.800
and I think people are very basic.

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:32.175
They look for a report or

00:08:32.175 --> 00:08:34.572
a very simple ad product

00:08:34.572 --> 00:08:36.191
to make them feel good,

00:08:36.191 --> 00:08:38.300
while underestimating when

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.880
tens of millions of people

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:41.450
are paying attention to something,

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.880
inevitably there's an
opportunity to monetize.

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:47.590
- There's a huge consumer
understanding gap

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:50.532
between Apple saying,

00:08:50.532 --> 00:08:54.110
we're improving the voice of Siri.

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:55.060
- I got it.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:56.864
I believe that if you look at history,

00:08:56.864 --> 00:08:59.839
it's usually a singular moment.

00:08:59.839 --> 00:09:03.740
A killer app, a singular moment,

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:07.879
so I believe there'll
be an Alexa skill built

00:09:07.879 --> 00:09:09.643
that is so phenomenal,

00:09:09.643 --> 00:09:11.900
that catches virality,

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.360
that makes everybody go,

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:14.617
oh crap, I need that.

00:09:14.617 --> 00:09:15.490
- Right.
- You know?

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.540
If you think back to the iPhone,

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:18.770
whether it was a social network,

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:20.103
whether it was Spotify,

00:09:20.103 --> 00:09:22.060
iTunes itself.
- Yeah.

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:23.760
- I would argue iTunes itself, right?

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.093
- Rest in peace.

00:09:26.667 --> 00:09:28.130
- Whether it was MySpace,

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:30.290
whether it was Tinder for dating,

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.550
I think there's a moment.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:33.170
And I think there'll be a killer app

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.630
or a functionality

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:39.100
that catches the national,
the global ecosystem

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:41.410
and the value prop will become obvious

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:42.440
and away we go.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:45.690
I remember eBay, looking
for wide awareness

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:47.260
in the late '90s.

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:51.789
It was Beanie Babies that
put so many people on eBay.

00:09:51.789 --> 00:09:54.366
I would say voice will have a Beanie,

00:09:54.366 --> 00:09:56.648
AR, it was Pokemon Go

00:09:56.648 --> 00:09:58.610
that allowed people to even

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.560
