00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:02.717
I believe there'll be
a singular voice moment

00:10:02.717 --> 00:10:05.550
that will trigger people saying,

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:06.632
wait a minute.

00:10:06.632 --> 00:10:09.766
I can do that on that instead of this?

00:10:09.766 --> 00:10:10.614
(snap)

00:10:10.614 --> 00:10:12.764
- Where do you see podcasting headed,

00:10:12.764 --> 00:10:16.340
and the creation of new
audio format as well?

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:17.610
- I mean, I think podcasting will

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:19.113
continue to massively grow.

00:10:19.113 --> 00:10:22.909
Which doesn't mean
individual shows will grow,

00:10:22.909 --> 00:10:25.190
because once there's many more shows,

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:26.747
there's only so much attention.

00:10:26.747 --> 00:10:28.963
But I think they will continue to grow.

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:32.320
And as far as new formats,

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:35.903
I think the next format is really

00:10:35.903 --> 00:10:38.500
skill-based audio

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.800
where we as humans are
interacting with audio.

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:45.680
Where we're actually doing
things through our voice

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:47.530
and a smart device on the other side.

00:10:47.530 --> 00:10:48.363
- Yeah.

00:10:48.363 --> 00:10:49.196
Could you give an example

00:10:49.196 --> 00:10:50.029
where that's useful?

00:10:50.029 --> 00:10:52.186
- Booking our plane through Alexa

00:10:52.186 --> 00:10:55.173
instead of Expedia on your phone.

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:57.973
Alexa, I want to go to Miami.

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:00.295
When would you like to go?

00:11:00.295 --> 00:11:01.530
Thursday, between

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:03.290
Can you look at my calendar,

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:05.500
and tell me the cheapest price

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:07.563
and the best time for me to go?

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:10.488
That is a far better experience

00:11:10.488 --> 00:11:14.281
because it's using information
from your calendar.

00:11:14.281 --> 00:11:17.985
That is much smarter than
my highest paid assistant,

00:11:17.985 --> 00:11:19.880
and is far faster.

00:11:19.880 --> 00:11:21.476
And that was a very simple example

00:11:21.476 --> 00:11:24.350
that is easily done by Google Home

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:26.930
by tapping into your Google calendar

